WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.770
The new "Frasier" series on Paramount+ brings
lots of new faces into Dr. Crane's life, including

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.720
a young mom with a tragic backstory named
Eve.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.860
But where may you have seen the actress who
plays her before?

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.450
The 2023 "Frasier" revival shares a name with
its predecessor, but its setting and timeframe

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.500
set the new show apart in plenty of key ways
from the classic '90s sitcom.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.910
The most important addition is Frasier Crane's
adult son Freddy.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.250
Frasier uproots himself to visit and eventually
live with his son in Boston at the series'

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:32.599
start, giving the revival an environment entirely
distinct from the iconic Seattle setting of

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:34.309
the original series.

00:00:34.309 --> 00:00:37.719
At the start of the first episode, Freddy
lives in an apartment with a friend of his

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:38.780
named Eve.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.420
Frasier initially assumes that Freddy and
Eve are in a relationship before learning

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.760
that Eve and her infant son moved in with
Freddy after the child's father — a firefighting

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.690
colleague of Freddy's — died on the job.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.829
"I don't need to be told who you are!"

00:00:51.829 --> 00:00:53.310
"I wish I could say the same!"

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.219
Jess Salgueiro plays Eve in the "Frasier"
revival.

00:00:56.219 --> 00:01:00.579
Her filmography before joining "Frasier" consists
largely of television work, including roles

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:03.739
in shows from the past decade that span a
variety of genres.

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:10.320
"Workin' Moms" aired on the CBC in Salgueiro's
home country of Canada between 2017 and 2023.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.190
Netflix carries the show for international
viewers.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.690
As the title implies, it follows a group of
mothers attempting to overcome the myriad

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:21.040
struggles of balancing an active career with
motherhood in an urban Toronto setting.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.270
Dani Kind's Anne Carlson is one of these moms.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:28.259
In Season 1, Anne decides that her daughter,
Alice, might benefit from some discipline

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:32.450
and hires a young woman with a stern demeanor,
played by Salgueiro, to babysit.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.530
The character takes on the nickname "Mean
Nanny…"

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:35.530
"'Mean Nanny'?"

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.439
"Yeah, that's what we call you.

00:01:37.439 --> 00:01:38.439
'Mean Nanny.'"

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:39.439
"I don't care.

00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:40.439
I kinda like it."

00:01:40.439 --> 00:01:44.040
…but she and Alice end up getting along,
undermining Anne's plan.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.759
Mean Nanny continues working for Anne and
becomes a recurring character through Seasons

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:48.899
2 and 3.

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:52.759
Her storyline reaches its dramatic apex when
Anne's best friend Kate finds out that her

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:56.680
husband Nathan is having an affair with Mean
Nanny near the end of Season 2.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:00.840
This affair, understandably, leads to Mean
Nanny's departure from the series.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.289
Salgueiro plays the character in a total of
12 episodes.

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:07.909
Canadian sitcom "Letterkenny" takes place
in the fictional Canadian small town of the

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:08.909
title.

00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:13.160
Frequently causing drama in the town of Letterkenny
are its hockey teams, including both the Letterkenny

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.740
Shamrocks and the Letterkenny Irish.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:19.940
Three of the show's core cast members, Reilly,
Jonesy, and Shoresy, play for both of these

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.400
teams at various points in the show.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.610
Season 5 introduces a women's hockey team
called the Letterkenny Shamrockettes.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:30.050
Throughout that team's periodic appearances,
its two key players are Betty-Anne, played

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:33.519
by Kelly McCormack, and Mary-Anne, played
by Salgueiro.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:37.160
In a May 2020 interview with Popternative,
Salgueiro said that she and McCormack had

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.670
such a good time on the "Letterkenny" set
that she left sore one day as a result of

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.720
nearly laughing during filming.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.000
Referring to "chirping," the show's term for
ribbing or mocking, she said,

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.349
"I remember leaving set one day, I think probably
our first time we ever did it, which was this

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:53.560
locker room scene where Betty-Anne and I are
chirping each other out.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.599
We left that day and I'm like, man I have
the worst chest pains.

00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:57.989
And I was like, what is this?

00:02:57.989 --> 00:02:59.780
Oh, it's holding in laughter.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.940
It's literally from me trying so hard not
to laugh."

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:06.720
"Who would have thought the girl who ingested
mosquito eggs after drinking out of mud puddles

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.819
would almost be accepted to community college?"

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:13.849
In the first episode of the satirical superhero
show "The Boys," protagonist Hughie Campbell's

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:18.770
partner Robin Ward, played by Salgueiro, dies
after Flash parody A-Train collides with her

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.330
at a high speed, killing her instantly.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.950
After her death, Robin retains a presence
in a few more episodes in Season 1.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.840
Hughie is so upset by her death that he joins
Billy Butcher as a member of the Boys organization,

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.340
which is devoted to stopping the world's overpowered
and egotistical superheroes.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.870
While he's still coming to terms with losing
her, Hughie is haunted by visions of Robin,

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:41.560
particularly after starting up a new relationship
with Starlight.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.239
Before long, though, Starlight helps him move
on.

00:03:44.239 --> 00:03:47.690
Salgueiro shared some insight into her brief
but impactful time working on "The Boys" in

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:50.019
a September 2019 interview with Collider.

00:03:50.019 --> 00:03:57.349
"I had a Spidey sense when I was reading these
scripts — I hadn't felt that way about anything

00:03:57.349 --> 00:03:58.349
I'd read."

00:03:58.349 --> 00:04:02.390
"The Expanse" aired on SYFY for three seasons
before its cancellation and subsequent return

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.360
as an Amazon original series.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:08.750
In the first Prime Video season of "The Expanse,"
Salgueiro debuted as Chandra Wei, who has

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:11.110
an amorous entanglement with Amos Burton.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:15.250
Complicating their interactions is her devotion
to her boss, Adolphus Murtry, who she credits

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.650
with saving her life.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.180
Chandra is relatively kindhearted, but Murtry
is outright evil.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.370
So, while Salgueiro maintains a central role
throughout Season 4 as a member of its main

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:28.259
cast, her character's association with the
villainous Murtry culminates with Amos having

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:31.240
to kill her, concluding her run on the series.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.890
Salgueiro told The Fearless Nomad in July
2022,

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:36.200
"I loved playing Chandra Wei on 'The Expanse.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.010
I love the complexity with which she was written.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:42.180
When something is written well I find that
the character sticks with me and is sometimes

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.100
incorporated into who I am.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.139
She's one of those."

00:04:45.139 --> 00:04:50.470
In 2020, Netflix adapted the novel "Tiny Pretty
Things" into an original TV series, the first

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.300
and only season of which hit the streaming
service in December of that year.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:58.160
It's mostly set at The Archer School of Ballet
in Chicago, which trains elite dancers but

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.150
hides some insidious secrets.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:03.880
Salgueiro plays Isabel, a former soldier working
as a Chicago cop.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:07.539
She's tasked with investigating the case of
Cassie Shore, a top dancer whose fall from

00:05:07.539 --> 00:05:12.100
the school roof is ruled an accident, but
which Isabel suspects was the result of foul

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.100
play.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.760
Salgueiro said of Isabel in a May 2021 interview,

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:18.030
"She had a hard go of it for sure.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:21.389
She was a dark character."

00:05:21.389 --> 00:05:25.060
She also mentioned that she filmed a brief
role in the Netflix superhero drama "Jupiter's

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:27.000
Legacy" at the same time.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.860
Between then and the "Frasier" reboot, Salgueiro
also worked on shows including "Y: The Last

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:34.710
Man" and "Sip," and did voice work for the
2021 video game "Far Cry 6."

